get  your bite out of the gutter recruit if  the tiny soldiers encounter another  container of play-doh or a similar model  clay it will also spring to life and  become a new army of tiny soldiers once  the army's out of the can they will  remain active until they've been stuffed  back inside now you've probably heard of  the guillotines used to execute the  powerful during the french revolution  scp-374 is one of these guillotines  constructed from an oak frame and a  sharp steel blade when used to execute a  human being something bizarre happens  the head of the victim becomes overtaken  by the personality of a man from the  french revolution named jean-philippe  haas donation for a duration of 35  minutes now pardon my fringe it is able  to answer questions during this time  though it tends to be uncooperative due  to its mistrust of the foundation which  considering it becomes conscious only  after a head is chopped off a human body  makes some sense then we have another  pistol but one that is nothing else like  we've seen today  scp-1998 is a pistol of unknown make and  model the peculiar thing about 1998 is  its lack of any ammunition rather than  firing any kind of bullets the gun fires  a pulse of energy from an undetermined  power source these pulses of energy have  no effect on a target that is not the  human body if it hits a human however it  has a notable effect on the brain  particularly the motor cortex the  primary auditory cortex and the  hippocampus  once someone has been hit three things  happen first the target turns and sits  down in front of the person wielding  scp-1998  then the target becomes paralyzed and  has no control over their physical  movement the target will then listen to  and believe anything the person firing  scp-1998 says to them the operator of  the weapon is then able to rewrite the  victim's memories and give them commands  which the victim will follow as closely  as possible as soon as they can move  again victims of  scp-1998 have described the effects of  the weapon as horrifically painful and  dramatic and that comes as no surprise  it is essentially a weapon that allows  its user to fight against free will  itself now get to work and remember as  you walk past the containment cells keep  your eyes to yourself you might see  something you don't want to see or  something that really really doesn't  want you to see it  now go check out  scp-3108 the nerfing gun and scp elite  mobile task force explained for more  combat and weaponry at the scp  foundation
 

